To create a colorful and interactive website, you can use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. First, let's start with the HTML structure, including the head, body, and title elements.
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
</head>
<body>
    <div id="joke-container">
        <div id="joke-header">
            <p>My Joke Website</p>
        </div>
        <div id="joke-footer">
            <p>Push to reveal punchline?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="joke-content">
            <p id="joke"></p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <script>
        // Replace the joke with a real joke when the button is clicked
        const button = document.getElementById('joke-toggle');
        button.addEventListener('click', function () {
            const joke = document.getElementById('joke').textContent;
            document.getElementById('joke').textContent = 'Punchline';
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```
